body:
I'm on Poetry version 1.2.0a2 and I've encountered this issue as well.

It appears to be caused by the mismatched signatures of [`pip_install`](https://github.com/python-poetry/poetry/blob/61301a195685608cc3ea95a9df2aaec049a27dce/poetry/utils/pip.py#L18) and [`pip_editable_install`](https://github.com/python-poetry/poetry/blob/61301a195685608cc3ea95a9df2aaec049a27dce/poetry/utils/pip.py#L63). The `upgrade` kwarg is passed to both functions [in executor.py](https://github.com/python-poetry/poetry/blob/61301a195685608cc3ea95a9df2aaec049a27dce/poetry/installation/executor.py#L129), but `pip_editable_install` doesn't take such an argument.

Adding an `upgrade` kwarg to `pip_editable_install` fixed the problem:
```python
def pip_editable_install(directory: Path, environment: Env, upgrade: bool = True) -> Union[int, str]:
    return pip_install(
        path=directory, environment=environment, editable=True, deps=False, upgrade=upgrade
    )
```
